  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 January 1930; the four outgoing councillors were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1930, p. 9). 'There will be no election in Cookstown, as the only nominations received by the returning officer, Mr. J. W. Fleming (Town Clerk), were those of the four outgoing councillors. Messrs. D. H. Hamilton (vice-chairman), Geo. Ferguson, Samuel M'Kinney, and J. M'D. Scott, who are therefore returned unopposed.' Returned unopposed."
